    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Brahmo Samaj was established in 1828, spearheaded by Raja Rammohan Roy to introduce socio-religious reforms.",
        "Arya Samaj was founded in 1875, emphasizing a return to Vedic teachings and social reform.",
        "Ramakrishna Mission was founded in 1897 by Swami Vivekananda to focus on spiritual revival and humanitarian service.",
        "Socio-religious reform movements encompassed Hindu, Muslim (Aligarh Movement), and Sikh communities alongside dedicated women's reform efforts."
